;; The parameters of the Fellegi-Sunter model the probabilistic engine of
;; `palomar reconcile` scores with by default (lot N2, ADR 0058 amendment).
;; `palomar.agent-match/model` computes the weights from them.
;;
;; They are the M4 model fitted on all five families of the M2 gold
;; (docs/eval/person-reconciliation.md, "A Fellegi-Sunter score (M4)"):
;; m from the 136 true pairs of 150 BnF INTERMARC records, u from the BnF
;; person pool against itself, the prior the share of true pairs among the
;; pairs the dates do not block. A test checks that the eval still fits
;; these numbers (`palomar.reconciliation-test`).
;;
;; IN-SAMPLE. It is fitted on every mention of M2 (`:provenance :split
;; :all-in-sample`): it must not score M2, nor any benchmark built from
;; those records or that pool. `palomar.reconciliation/refuse-in-sample!`
;; refuses it on that pool (as the eval reads it, `:pool`, or as
;; `read-authorities` does, `:pool-as-read`) and on those records (by their
;; SHA-256); the eval calls it.
;;
;; Derived from BnF data: Licence Ouverte / Etalab 2.0, "Source :
;; Bibliothèque nationale de France" (see NOTICE).
;;
;; The model is not calibrated: it carries no `:calibration` report, so no
;; posterior it gives is ever written as a confidence. Every true pair it
;; learnt from is an exact heading; read its limits in the eval.
;;
;; Lot O4 (ADR 0062): its weights follow the rules it states (`:rules`: the
;; form weighs only on an exact name; the chain of name weights runs over the
;; measured levels). It states no `:gap`: a second candidate at or above the
;; review threshold always competes.
;;
;; The run manifest names the model by its version (`model-version`): the
;; SHA-256 of its parameters as read, and the fingerprint of its weights. A
;; comment or a layout change is no new version; a changed parameter is.
{:prior 0.12890995260663507
 :thresholds {:propose 0.95 :review 0.5}
 :rules {:form :exact-name :chain :measured-levels}
 :bar {:max-ece 0.05 :max-bin-gap 0.1 :min-pairs 300 :min-positives 100 :min-review-pairs 30 :bins 10}
 :m-counts {:name {:n 136.0 :counts {:exact 136.0}}
            :form {:n 136.0 :counts {:heading 136.0}}
            :dates {:n 136.0 :counts {:agree 131.0 :unknown 5.0}}}
 :u-counts {:name {:n 1056.0 :counts {:none 856.0 :jaccard-high 30.0 :jaccard-low 146.0 :exact 2.0
                                      :forenames-differ 10.0 :forename-overlap 12.0}}
            :form {:n 1056.0 :counts {:heading 1042.0 :variant 14.0}}
            :dates {:n 264.0 :counts {:unknown 244.0 :agree 20.0}}}
 :estimation {:m :supervised :trained-on ["Dumas" "Hetzel" "Hugo" "Verne" "others"]}
